From 6db741fbd0b9d9f7eabce4e7b135f94cd8b4159a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:05:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Direct control guests: the local chain verifier as a
 HOST_DATA-bound config member, started before the direct supervisor

metal/guest/measured-control.mjs: canonicalDirectConfig takes an optional chainVerifier member (the relay-mode checker:
explicit https proof sources, the sequencer pin, port 50000..57999 distinct from every other port of the config, optional
own txBackend). Absent, every earlier config keeps its exact canonical bytes and digest; present, it is bound by HOST_DATA.
directSupervisorEnv gives the supervisor the chain-authority names from that member only (flavor and host-policy input
for them is dropped). planDirectBoot refuses the boot when the image carries no verifier runtime, and otherwise returns
the launch; the hosted MCP adapter's profile gets the same verifier (A's existing chainVerifier field); the statement
names the image's runtime record (runtime.chainVerifierImageSha256, the existing runtime-hash convention).
metal/guest/gsup.mjs: the direct branch starts the bound verifier as its supervised child before the direct supervisor.
metal/enclave-metal.mjs: a host-level chainVerifier for a direct guest still refuses, now saying it belongs in the bound
direct config. The controller identity, admission, pins and the required rpcs field are unchanged; nothing goes through
a relay.
docs/network/local-chain-verifier.md: the guest section covers direct guests, the own backend and the consumers.
